-- #964 regression fixture — the def list is a SET of sites, never a bag.
--
-- Read test/references_fixtures/dup_field_def/expected.golden as the assertion:
-- NO `DEF` column here may list the same `main.mdk:<line>:<col>` twice.
--
-- Why this is not hypothetical. `defsOfDecl` (compiler/tools/refindex.mdk) records
-- a record FIELD once PER VARIANT, every one at the enclosing `data` decl's single
-- name `Loc`, and every one under `mkKey mid nsField fn` — which carries NO variant
-- discriminator. So a field name shared by K variants is recorded K times at
-- byte-identical spans. `frontend/ast.mdk`'s own `Decl` does exactly this: its
-- `DInterface` and `DImpl` variants each declare `pub` and `methods`.
--
-- The last-write-wins `hmSet` this fixture's sibling (#964) replaced happened to be
-- idempotent under that, so accumulating def sites re-exposed it. It matters because
-- two edits over an IDENTICAL range in one LSP `WorkspaceEdit` are rejected by strict
-- clients and DOUBLE-APPLIED by lenient ones (`labellabel`) — silent source
-- corruption, the class #964 exists to close.

-- S0-1: `x` is declared by BOTH variants, at one decl Loc, under one field key.
-- Its DEF column must hold exactly ONE site.
export data T =
  | A { x : Int }
  | B { x : Int }

-- S0-2: three variants sharing `tag` — a bag would show the site three times.
export data U =
  | U1 { tag : String }
  | U2 { tag : String }
  | U3 { tag : String }

-- Control: `only` belongs to a single variant, so its ONE def site proves the
-- golden distinguishes "deduplicated" from "collapsed to one no matter what".
export data V =
  | V1 { only : Int }
  | V2 { other : Int }

export mkA : Int -> T
mkA n = A { x = n }

export getX : T -> Int
getX t = t.x

-- ⚠️ `getX` ABOVE NO LONGER TYPECHECKS, AND THAT IS FINE HERE — but it is worth
-- saying, because it stopped being a working program during #1455's round-2 review
-- and nothing in this fixture's own gate would tell you.  `t.x` selects through a
-- `T`-typed receiver and `T` has TWO named-field constructors, so the selection names
-- no constructor and is now refused (`T-FIELD-VARIANT-CONFLICT`).  It was never
-- portable: MEASURED on a cold build of the merge base `bfcd4ea7`, native printed
-- `t=1,2` while the WasmGC build TRAPPED at instantiation with `illegal cast` — on
-- WasmGC a record is a struct type PER CONSTRUCTOR, so the stamp is a cast.
--
-- This file is kept BYTE-IDENTICAL above this line anyway, deliberately.
-- `diff_compiler_references_correctness.sh` dumps the REFERENCE INDEX (resolve +
-- index); it never typechecks, so the dump is unaffected — verified by running the
-- gate on this exact file with the new compiler.  And the `.x` occurrence is the ONLY
-- thing in the fixture that produces a `field|x` USE: rewriting it as a record PATTERN
-- was tried and dropped the golden's `main|field|x` row to `USES 0`, weakening the very
-- cell #964 added.  Every pinned `main.mdk:LINE:COL` in expected.golden is at or above
-- line 41, so this note cannot move one.
